# crontab for claude-pulse (run `crontab -e` and paste, adjusting paths).
#
# Each tick just *evaluates*; the policy engine gates the actual poke, so a
# 10-minute cadence simply means "poke promptly once idle long enough".
#
# Find your entry point:  which claude-pulse   (or use: python3 -m claude_pulse)

*/10 * * * * $HOME/.local/bin/claude-pulse tick >> $HOME/.claude-pulse/cron.log 2>&1

# If installed only as a module (not on PATH), use the interpreter form:
# */10 * * * * /usr/bin/python3 -m claude_pulse tick >> $HOME/.claude-pulse/cron.log 2>&1
